          "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a diagram in a category\n<MATH_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Assume the index category <MATH_0003> is filtered and\nlet <MATH_0004> be a cocone for <MATH_0005>, see\nRemark <REF_0001>. We say <MATH_0006> is\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>essentially constant<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> with <TEXTITOPEN_0002>value<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> <MATH_0007> if there exist an\n<MATH_0008> and a morphism <MATH_0009> such that\n<STRUCT_0003>\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0010> is <MATH_0011>, and\n<STRUCT_0005> for all <MATH_0012> there exist <MATH_0013> and morphisms <MATH_0014> and <MATH_0015>\nsuch that the morphism <MATH_0016> equals the composition\n<MATH_0017>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n<STRUCT_0007> Assume the index category <MATH_0018> is cofiltered and let\n<MATH_0019> be a cone for <MATH_0020>, see\nRemark <REF_0002>. We say\n<MATH_0021> is <TEXTITOPEN_0003>essentially constant<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> with <TEXTITOPEN_0004>value<TEXTITCLOSE_0004> <MATH_0022> if\nthere exist an <MATH_0023>\nand a morphism <MATH_0024> such that\n<STRUCT_0008>\n<STRUCT_0009> <MATH_0025> is <MATH_0026>, and\n<STRUCT_0010> for all <MATH_0027> there exist <MATH_0028> and morphisms <MATH_0029> and <MATH_0030>\nsuch that the morphism <MATH_0031> equals the composition\n<MATH_0032>.\n<STRUCT_0011>\n<STRUCT_0012>\nPlease keep in mind Lemma <REF_0003>\nwhen using this definition.\n",
